{
  "id": "COMPOUND:549 - DISEASE:2613",
  "verbalization": "Methotrexate appears to influence multiple pathways that ultimately contribute to the development of Postoperative Nausea and Vomiting (PONV). The evidence suggests that Methotrexate affects genes involved in phospholipid transport (via the armadillo repeat containing X-linked 3 gene) and in the regulation of protein folding (via the GLI family zinc finger 1 gene), both of which may play roles in gastrointestinal function and motility. These mechanisms could disrupt normal physiological processes, leading to nausea and vomiting. Additionally, Methotrexate's effect on adrenoceptor alpha 1D may indirectly contribute to PONV by influencing immune responses, as indicated by the chain of causation involving immunoglobulin kappa variable 3-34 (pseudogene). While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the integrated evidence points to a complex interplay of genetic and signaling pathways that may be targeted by Methotrexate to modulate PONV.",
